From: Stereolabs <embedded@stereolabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] host1x: fix race in syncpt alloc/free (kref_put_mutex)

host1x_syncpt_put() did kref_put() then syncpt_release() separately
acquired syncpt_mutex; in that window host1x_syncpt_alloc() (scanning
for kref_read()==0 under the mutex) could grab the slot being released
and kref_init() it, after which syncpt_release() kfree()'d sp->name /
freed the base of the live new allocation (UAF / double-free /
syncpoint reused before fully released). Use kref_put_mutex() so the
mutex is held atomically across the zero-refcount window.
Backport of torvalds c7d393267c497502fa737607f435f05dfe6e3d9b.
Ported to R36.5 (unchanged NVIDIA baseline vs R36.4).
---
diff --git a/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c b/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c
index 6a01771..2664414 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c
@@ -414,8 +414,6 @@ static void syncpt_release(struct kref *ref)
 
 	sp->locked = false;
 
-	mutex_lock(&sp->host->syncpt_mutex);
-
 	host1x_syncpt_base_free(sp->base);
 	kfree(sp->name);
 	sp->base = NULL;
@@ -438,7 +436,7 @@ void host1x_syncpt_put(struct host1x_syncpt *sp)
 	if (!sp)
 		return;
 
-	kref_put(&sp->ref, syncpt_release);
+	kref_put_mutex(&sp->ref, syncpt_release, &sp->host->syncpt_mutex);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(host1x_syncpt_put);
 
